      "text": "To determine the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the prime factorization of both numbers:**\n   - For 342:\n     \\[\n     342 \\div 2 = 171 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 2^1 \\times 171\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     171 \\div 3 = 57 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3^2 \\times 57\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     57 \\div 3 = 19 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3^3 \\times 19\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     19 \\quad \\text{(a prime number)} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3^3 \\times 19\n     \\]\n     Therefore, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n     \\[\n     342 = 2^1 \\times 3^3 \\times 19^1\n     \\]\n\n   - For 285:\n     \\[\n     285 \\div 3 = 95 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3^1 \\times 95\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     95 \\div 5 = 19 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 5^1 \\times 19\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     19 \\quad \\text{(a prime number)} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3^1 \\times 5^1 \\times 19^1\n     \\]\n     Therefore, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n     \\[\n     285 = 3^1 \\times 5^1 \\times 19^1\n     \\]\n\n2. **Identify common prime factors and their minimum powers:**\n   The common prime factors of 342 and 285 are 3, 5, and 19. The minimum power of 3 in both factorizations is \\(3^1\\), the minimum power of 5 is \\(5^1\\), and 19 remains \\(19^1\\).\n\n3. **Multiply the common prime factors raised to their minimum powers:**\n   The largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is given by:\n   \\[\n   3^1 \\times 5^1 \\times 19^1 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the product:**\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 5 = 15\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   15 \\times 19 = 285\n   \\]\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{285}\\).",
